# This repository compares exact bytes everywhere: the emitter round-trip
# gate on backlog/knowledge JSON, the golden suites, and the root-vs-template
# parity tests, on every OS. No checkout may convert line endings anywhere,
# so every path is `-text`; the more specific lines below stay as emphasis
# for the especially-critical trees.
* -text

# The frozen fixture corpus (tests/corpus/) is byte-compared verbatim by
# the Rust parity gate. `-text` disables Git's line-ending conversion on
# checkin and checkout for these paths regardless of core.autocrlf, so a
# Windows checkout (the CI matrix's windows-latest leg) keeps the
# committed bytes exactly, instead of translating them to CRLF and
# breaking every byte compare.
tests/corpus/** -text

# The reviewed, Rust-generated goldens (tests/goldens/) are byte-compared
# the same way the frozen corpus is (render_parity.rs, check_parity.rs,
# read_parity.rs). Same reason as above: `-text` keeps the committed
# bytes exact on every checkout.
tests/goldens/** -text

# The fixture directories under tests/fixtures/ (mini, mini-bad,
# mini-stale, batch14-workspace, invalid-deliverable, skipped-report,
# stats-workspace) are compared exact-string by check_parity.rs (its
# stale-generated-file compare and byte/line budget checks) and the
# other parity tests. Same reason as above: `-text` keeps the committed
# bytes exact on every checkout.
tests/fixtures/** -text

# This repository's own generated knowledge surface -- render_all()'s
# output set (render.rs: RULE_KINDS's per-area .claude/rules/*.md files,
# standing-rules.md, and the fixed SKILL_PATH) -- is compared
# exact-string by dogfood.rs's freshness check (`houserules render
# --check` against this checkout's own live root). Same reason as above:
# `-text` keeps the committed bytes exact on every checkout.
.claude/rules/** -text
.claude/skills/project-knowledge/** -text

# The embedded install payload (crates/houserules/src/install.rs) walks
# template/ at compile time and bakes its exact checkout bytes into the
# binary. `-text` keeps every checkout of template/ LF regardless of the
# build host's core.autocrlf, so every build embeds the same bytes and a
# seeded install passes the emitter round-trip gate on every OS.
template/** -text
